# AWNIC review scrapers — cron schedule
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste both lines, fixed to your VM path)

# Own reviews — every 90 minutes (cron can't do */90, so two lines give an
# exact 90-min cadence: fires at 00:00, 01:30, 03:00, 04:30 ... 22:30)
0  0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21 * * * /home/user_sai/GoogleReviewsLogger/deploy/run_reviews.sh
30 1,4,7,10,13,16,19,22 * * * /home/user_sai/GoogleReviewsLogger/deploy/run_reviews.sh

# Competitor reviews — once a day at 06:00 (13 competitor places per run)
0 6 * * * /home/user_sai/GoogleReviewsLogger/deploy/run_competitors.sh

# NOTES
# - 90-min own polling = 16 actor runs/day; competitors add 13 place-scrapes
#   once daily. Watch Apify usage.
# - Dedup means only NEW/changed own reviews hit Groq; competitor reviews skip
#   Groq entirely (raw log), so the daily competitor run is cheap.
# - flock guards in both run scripts prevent overlapping runs.
# - Own logs:        logs/reviews_YYYY-MM-DD.log
#   Competitor logs: logs/competitors_YYYY-MM-DD.log
# - Verify paths with:  realpath deploy/run_reviews.sh deploy/run_competitors.sh
